      "title": "[agrobiznes.ro] Romanian agency extends small-farm grant deadline to Nov. 16",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://agrobiznes.ro/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/floricultura-afir.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nRomania’s Agency for Financing Rural Investments has extended application deadlines for two farm-investment programs — DR-14 for small farms and DR-18 for floriculture and medicinal and aromatic plants — from Oct. 31 to Nov. 16, 2026, at 4 p.m. The extension applies only to components with funds remaining; the DR-14 simple-purchases component closed Oct. 6 after exhausting its budget.\n\nUnder DR-14, eligible small farms can seek grants of up to €50,000 per project, covering up to 85% of eligible costs. Farmers have until Nov. 16 to submit proposals under the components that remain open.",
